00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:03.429 align:start position:0%
molden district council collects your  council tax  and puts it in a separate fund called  the collection fund  we share this fund with essex county  council  essex police fire and crime commissioner  and  the parish and town councils this year  we need to collect 47 million pounds in  council tax  every one pound of council tax is shared  in the following way  essex county council receives 71 pence  malden district council receive 11 pence  essex police fire and crime commissioner  for policing and community safety  receive 11 pence essex police fire and  crime commissioner for fire and rescue  service  receive four pence parish and town  councils receive  three pence essex county council use  council tax to pay for services such as  social services highways and libraries  molden district council use council tax  to help pay for services such as  planning leisure services collecting  waste and recycling  molden district council has increased  its 2021-22  council tax charges by 2.5 percent  this sees a band d charge increase from  202 pounds 40  to 207 pounds 40 an increase of 5 pounds  over the year  equivalent to an additional 9.6 p per  week  how much do you have to pay we work out  your council tax after totaling the  money  each of the four authorities require if  for example your home is in bandi  the average council tax for this year  will be 1830 pounds  73 plus an amount you have to pay to  your local parish  or town council for more information  search for council tax at molden.gov dot  uk
 

